      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 2</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>During 2024, Servicing Every Soul launched new educational programming focused on regenerative agriculture and aquaponics, supported by the Prebys Foundation's "Healing Through Nature" grant. The ranch hosted hands-on youth education days, volunteer land restoration projects, and community workshops introducing sustainable farming practices.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 3</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The organization expanded its existing land stewardship activities into a more structured education model, formalizing partnerships with local schools and nonprofit organizations. Operations scaled significantly due to new grant funding and increased volunteer participation, with improved documentation, evaluation, and program reporting processes.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 2</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Many board members are related. The organization is a family-founded nonprofit. All related directors serve without compensation except for one board member (who also served as Executive Director).</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 4</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>During 2024, Servicing Every Soul updated its bylaws to clarify officer duties, quorum requirements, and voting procedures. No structural or mission changes were made.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The preparer sent the form with the Board via email and received suggested updates via email.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The Board reviewed the suggested compensation and decided to offer a below-market rate for the Executive Director in alignment with what the organization could afford at the time. The ED understood, as they were also a Board Member privy to the organization's financials, and accepted the compensation.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
